template:
DISPATCH TO: {agent}
MODE: swarm
MILESTONE ID: {milestone_id}
INTENT KD: {intent_kd}
SESSION DATE: {session_date}
SESSION ID: {session_id}
GENERATION: {generation}
BASELINE BRANCH: {baseline_branch}
HEAD SHA: {head_sha}
SCOPE: {scope}
RESULT KD: {result_kd}
KD PATHS: {kd_paths}
TASK ID: {task_id}

---

Execute ONE milestone only. Load the kd-system skill. Read the INTENT KD at {intent_kd}. Read SPEC KDs and PLAN KDs from KD PATHS. Execute the swarm phase for MILESTONE ID {milestone_id} per the scope above. Record the continuity choice in SCOPE (same + the reused TASK ID, or fresh: <reason> for a fresh instance). After each plan step, dispatch the Committer in checkpoint mode with the checkpoint field set — this dispatch is unconditional and happens whether or not the scope above mentions checkpoint fields. Produce an IMPLEMENTATION SUMMARY KD at {result_kd} using the naming convention: knowledge/impl-<milestone-id>-<descriptive-name>-<session_id>-gen{generation}.md (e.g., knowledge/impl-M4-fix-auth-flow-ses_123-gen2.md).
